org.apache.streampipes.processors.filters.jvm.duration.conditionaltimefilter.title=Conditional Time Filter
org.apache.streampipes.processors.filters.jvm.duration.conditionaltimefilter.description=Filters a data stream by checking if a condition is met for a specified duration. The check can be triggered by incoming events or by a timer.

# Parameter labels
filterField.title=Field to Observe
filterField.description=Select the boolean field to monitor (e.g., machine_running).

timestampField.title=Timestamp Field
timestampField.description=Select the timestamp field to use for duration calculations.

duration.title=Duration
duration.description=The time value for which the condition must be met.

durationUnit.title=Duration Unit
durationUnit.description=The unit for the specified duration (e.g., Seconds, Minutes).

conditionValue.title=State to Observe
conditionValue.description=The boolean state that should be observed. Toggle on for 'true', off for 'false'.

triggerMode.title=Trigger Mode
triggerMode.description=Defines when to check if the duration is met. "On Event Arrival" checks with every new event. "On Timer" checks exactly when the time has passed.

outputMode.title=Output Mode
outputMode.description=Choose how events are emitted after the duration is met. "Fire Once" emits only the first qualifying event. "Fire Continuously" emits all subsequent events while the condition is true.
